    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite builds green with a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), which now confirms the `fiscalYear` field.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July) with low structural impact \u2014 a new self-contained helper carries the logic, so the three touchpoints each changed by a single line.\n\n**New file \u2014 `OwnerFiscalYearPolicy.java`**: A small, cohesive unit with two pure static methods:\n- `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 the fiscal year a date falls in (July\u2013December belongs to the *following* calendar year), the one shared derivation.\n- `fiscalYear(Owner)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` label from the business-day-adjusted registration date (null when absent).\n\n**Wiring (one line each, keeping every edited method simple):**\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 added a `fiscalYear` `@Mapping` expression alongside the existing derived-field mappings.\n- `OwnerMembershipPolicy.membershipNumber` \u2014 the `-M<YY>` segment now uses `fiscalYearOf(registrationDate)` instead of the raw calendar year.\n- `OwnerMembershipLevelPolicy.exceedsTenure` \u2014 tenure is now counted as elapsed fiscal years (`> 1`) rather than a 365-day window; the constant and unused `ChronoUnit` import were adjusted accordingly.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` schema property (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it) and refreshed the affected descriptions/examples.\n\nThe heavy `OwnerMembershipLevelPolicy` class (high WMC) was touched at only its one smallest method, and no method or class was grown \u2014 all new behaviour lives in the small new policy.\n\nNote on the fiscal-year convention: a date is labelled by the calendar year its fiscal year *ends* in (e.g. 2026-09-03 \u2192 `FY27`). The same `fiscalYearOf` drives the label, the membership number's `YY`, and tenure, so all three stay consistent. The acceptance test only pins the `FY\\d{2}` format; if your spec intends the *starting*-year convention instead, that's a one-line change in `fiscalYearOf`.",
